{
  "id": "gedalja",
  "name": "Gedaliah",
  "title": "Governor over Judah",
  "era": "exile",
  "lifespan": "c. 586 BC",
  "summary": "Gedaliah, son of Ahikam and grandson of Shaphan, was appointed by the Babylonian king Nebuchadnezzar as governor over the remaining inhabitants of Judah after the fall of Jerusalem in 586 BC. He ruled from Mizpah and encouraged the people to submit to the Babylonians to live peacefully, but was murdered by Ishmael son of Nethaniah, a man of royal descent. His killing led the remaining Jews to flee to Egypt against the advice of the prophet Jeremiah.",
  "roles": [
    "leader"
  ],
